  "name": "Knight",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>The few, the proud, the knights are martial characters dedicated to restoring the ideals of knightly chivalry before they fade forever. The knights see moral decay everywhere they look in the world around them, brought on by a lapse in ethical behavior. Knights adhere to a rigid code of behavior that embraces such values as honor, honesty, chivalry, and courage. The first duty of knights is to this code and the ideals for which it stands, rather to a holy order. A knight is expected to display these ideals in all aspects of his behavior throughout all his actions and deeds, however arduous they may be.</em></p><h2>Role</h2><p>The knight class embodies the steadfast defender and chivalrous protector, forming the unyielding bulwark of any adventuring party. Clad in heavy armor and wielding formidable weapons, their primary role is to stand firm on the front lines, drawing enemy aggression through abilities like taunting from intimidation, and soaking up damage that would otherwise overwhelm squishier allies like mages and healers.</p><p>Their toolkit often includes defensive stances, damage reduction buffs, and even abilities to intercept attacks aimed at others, embodying true self-sacrifice. Beyond raw defense, the knight frequently provides an aura of leadership and resolve, inspiring their comrades and often possessing skills that bolster party morale or provide minor utility. They are the paragon of valor and duty, ensuring the party's survival and creating the crucial space and breathing room for others to unleash their full potential, making them an indispensable cornerstone of any adventuring group.</p><h2>Class Skills</h2><p>The knight's class skills are Acrobatics (Dex), Climb (Str), Craft (Int), Diplomacy (Cha), Handle Animal (Cha), Intimidate (Cha), Knowledge (nobility) (Int), Perception (Wis), Profession (Wis), Ride (Dex), Sense Motive (Wis), and Swim (Str).</p><h2>Weapon and Armor Proficiency</h2><p>A knight is proficient with all simple and martial weapons (including knight swords) and with all armor (light, medium, and heavy) and shields (including tower shields).</p><h2>Main Ability Score</h2><p>The knight mainly focuses on Strength for martial combat, Constitution for their class features, and Charisma for optional features.</p><h2>Code of Conduct</h2><p>A knight must be of any lawful alignment and cannot level further into this class if he shifts to a chaotic alignment.</p><p>Additionally, a knight's code requires that he respect legitimate authority and act with honor (not lying, not cheating, not using poison, and so forth).</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
